# CODEOWNERS for arbsec/orchestraitor
#
# Orchestraitor delegates ALL security enforcement to Arbitraitor (arbsec/arbitraitor).
# No Orchestraitor crate may own security-decision logic (spec §2.2, §16.6), so CODEOWNERS
# routes by integration surface and governance concern, not by a separate security crate.

# Repo governance + workflow automation belong to the project-manager agent and maintainers.
/.github/                     @arbsec/maintainers
/.agents/                     @arbsec/maintainers
/AGENTS.md                    @arbsec/maintainers
/CONTRIBUTING.md              @arbsec/maintainers
/SECURITY.md                  @arbsec/maintainers
/GOVERNANCE.md                @arbsec/maintainers
/docs/spec/                   @arbsec/maintainers

# Dependency + license policy is security-sensitive regardless of where the lockfile lives.
/Cargo.lock                   @arbsec/security
/deny.toml                    @arbsec/security

# The Arbitraitor integration boundary is the most security-sensitive path in Orchestraitor.
# Every change here MUST be reviewed as security-sensitive (AGENTS.md).
/crates/orchestraitor-arbitraitor-client/  @arbsec/security

# Provider transports + the provider proxy handle secrets and untrusted protocol input.
/crates/orchestraitor-provider-api/        @arbsec/security
/crates/orchestraitor-provider-proxy/      @arbsec/security

# Normalization runs untrusted tool output through formatters/fixers; review carefully.
/crates/orchestraitor-workspace/           @arbsec/maintainers
